- **true**: Activated.
- **false**: Not activated.', example='true', position='Body'),
  opsUserCode?: string(name='opsUserCode', description='The proxy user code, which is unique within the tenant. This parameter is used only when the application credential is configured as source_uid.', example='alice', position='Query'),
  opsUserId?: string(name='opsUserId', description='The proxy user ID, which is the WINNEXO platform user ID. This parameter is used only when the application credential is configured as winnexo_uid.', example='10001', position='Query'),
  roleCodes?: [ string ](name='roleCodes', description='The new list of system role codes. This list fully replaces the existing roles and must contain at least one role. Valid values: SUPER_ADMIN, SYSTEM_ADMIN, SEMANTIC_ADMIN, SKILL_ADMIN, KB_ADMIN, AGENT_ADMIN, and APPLICATION_USER.', example='["APPLICATION_USER"]', shrink='json', position='Body'),
  tenantId?: string(name='tenantId', description='The ID of the effective tenant.', example='10000', position='Query'),
  userGroupIds?: [ string ](name='userGroupIds', description='The new list of user group IDs. This list fully replaces the existing user groups. If this parameter is not specified, the user groups are not modified.', example='["string_value"]', shrink='json', position='Body'),
  wnUserId: string(name='wnUserId', description='The ID of the target user, which is the WINNEXO platform user ID.

This parameter is required.', example='1', position='Body'),
}

model UpdateUserResponseBody = {
  code?: string(name='code', description='The error code.', example='200'),
  message?: string(name='message', description='The status code description.', example='ok'),
  requestId?: string(name='requestId', description='The request ID.', example='019FF406-1B10-0065-A97D-2D1920C2A03D'),
  wnUserId?: string(name='wnUserId', description='The WINNEXO platform user ID.', example='1'),
}

model UpdateUserResponse = {
  headers?: map[string]string(name='headers'),
  statusCode?: int32(name='statusCode'),
  body?: UpdateUserResponseBody(name='body'),
}

/**
  * @description Modifies user information.
  *     Workflow:
  *     1. Parse roleCodes into role_ids.
  *     2. If isActive changes, switch the status first, including protection for the last super administrator.
  *     3. Call update_tenant_member to modify other fields such as displayName, roleCodes, and userGroupIds.
  *     4. Return HTTP 200 if all steps succeed.
  *     Execution sequence:
  *     - The isActive status change is written before other fields. The two steps are not in the same transaction.
  *     - If validation fails, such as protection for the last super administrator, an exception is thrown and subsequent steps are not executed.
  *     - If the isActive change is persisted to the database but a subsequent step throws an exception, the isActive change is not rolled back.
  * @param request  the request parameters of UpdateUser  UpdateUserRequest
  * @return UpdateUserResponse
 */
async function updateUser(request: UpdateUserRequest): UpdateUserResponse {
  @handler.validateRequestModel(request);
  return @handler.do('RESTFUL', 'UpdateUser', 'POST', '/openapi/updateUser', 'json', true, 'form', request);
}

